## 1. Scene tree — exact structure

Main scene (`ChairScene.tscn`)

```
ChairScene (Node3D)
├── Chair (inherited from Chair.tscn)
├── DirectionalLight3D
└── Camera3D [Camera.gd]
```

Chair model scene (`Chair.tscn`)

```
Chair (Node3D) [chair_rotate.gd]
├── Cube
├── Cube.001
├── Cube.002
├── Cube.003
├── Cube.004
└── Cube.005
```

The cube children are the individual parts of the chair imported from Blender. Your exact imported child names may differ.

## 2. Blender — chair model

Create the chair using cubes.

| Part     | Operation  | Values |
| -------- | ---------- | ------ |
| Seat     | Scale Z    | `0.2`  |
| Seat     | Scale X    | `1.2`  |
| Seat     | Scale Y    | `1.2`  |
| Seat     | Location Z | `1`    |
| Leg      | Scale X    | `0.1`  |
| Leg      | Scale Y    | `0.1`  |
| Leg      | Scale Z    | `1`    |
| Leg      | Location Z | `0.5`  |
| Backrest | Scale X    | `1.2`  |
| Backrest | Scale Y    | `0.1`  |
| Backrest | Scale Z    | `1.2`  |
| Backrest | Location Z | `1.8`  |
| Backrest | Location Y | `0.65` |

For the four legs, position them at the seat corners using duplication (`Shift + D`) and movement along X and Y.

Export: `File → Export → glTF 2.0` and save as `chair.glb`.

